    },
    {
      "text": "Toss gently to coat the feta and sun-dried tomatoes in the herbs and oil.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/five-minute-marinated-feta-sun-dried-tomato-salad/#wprm-recipe-52599-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/lemon-herb-chicken-salad-w-creamy-rosemary-vinegarette-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Allow the feta to marinate while you wash and prep your greens, about four to five minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/five-minute-marinated-feta-sun-dried-tomato-salad/#wprm-recipe-52599-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/lemon-herb-chicken-salad-w-creamy-rosemary-vinegarette-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a large bowl, or two smaller bowls, plate your greens and top with the marinated feta and slivered almonds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/five-minute-marinated-feta-sun-dried-tomato-salad/#wprm-recipe-52599-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/lemon-herb-chicken-salad-w-creamy-rosemary-vinegarette-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drizzle the remaining olive oil and the lemon juice over the greens, then toss to coat. Season with salt and pepper to taste!",
